==============================================================================
H4 (ARNOLD CAT MAP): band twist e->s*e mod 7 as a toral automorphism
==============================================================================
  (a) multiplier e->s*e on Z/7: it is in (Z/7)^* (cyclic order 6).
      multiplier orders mod 7: {1: 1, 2: 3, 3: 6, 4: 3, 5: 6, 6: 2}  (all finite => ELLIPTIC, periodic, NOT hyperbolic)
      => the band twist is a TORSION rotation, not an Anosov cat map. (analogy-killer)
  (b) golden-slope CF renormalization matrix (period [1,1]) = [[2, 1], [1, 1]]
      trace=3, det=1, discriminant=5; |trace|>2 => HYPERBOLIC (this IS Arnold's cat map).
  (c) LRC cover breakpoints are RATIONAL (x=(7j+k)/(7e)); the band-mixing renormalization
      is x->7x mod 1: EXPANDING Bernoulli (entropy log 7), det 7 != +-1 => NOT a toral
      automorphism. The cat map requires a unimodular (det=+-1) gluing; the apex prime
      gives an expanding endomorphism instead. So: SHIFT/Bernoulli yes, CAT MAP no.

  H4 VERDICT: the renormalization is an EXPANDING base-7 endomorphism (a Bernoulli shift on
  7 symbols = the 7 bands), NOT a hyperbolic toral automorphism. Arnold's cat map is the
  WRONG dynamical analogy; the right one is the full 7-shift (subshift of finite type).

